An optional property whose scalar default is not the zero value keeps its plain
type when its schema excludes the zero value, as the committed
ElicitationSchema.type does: mode's enumeration and kind's single const hold no
"", so "" is never valid to send, and omitempty loses nothing
(0049-MADR-remediate-the-2026-11-01-debugging-pass.md, G6, Q22 a).

-- meta.json --
{"version": 1, "agentMethods": {}, "clientMethods": {}, "protocolMethods": {"cancel_request": "$/cancel_request"}}
-- schema.json --
{"$defs": {
  "Mode": {"type": "string", "enum": ["auto", "manual"]},
  "Kind": {"oneOf": [{"type": "string", "const": "object"}]},
  "Opts": {"type": "object", "properties": {
    "mode": {"allOf": [{"$ref": "#/$defs/Mode"}], "default": "auto"},
    "kind": {"allOf": [{"$ref": "#/$defs/Kind"}], "default": "object"}}},
  "CancelRequestNotification": {"type": "object", "x-side": "protocol", "x-method": "$/cancel_request"}
}}
